// A hypothetical breaking release of Leyline, written as a server migration.
// The model sources describe 2026-11-01 only. This file says how to serve
// clients still on 2026-09-04 from it. The compiler replays these steps on
// the frozen artifact releases/2026-09-04/leyline.model.json and refuses to
// build unless the result is the current model.
//
// Step verbs are a closed set. A step converts automatically, or names a hook:
// `by hook` generates a pure function, `by async hook` one that may do I/O.
// The compiler knows whether a shape is used in requests, responses or both,
// and generates only the directions that are needed.

/// Graph storage is reported as one structure, region becomes a required
/// choice, and graphs being deleted get their own status.
migration "2026-11-01" from "2026-09-04" {

    // ---- automatic ---------------------------------------------------------

    /// Renamed to match the api-standards common terms.
    rename GraphData.manifestGeneration -> generation

    /// Index kind is now required. Requests from older clients mean a B-tree.
    require CreateIndex.input.kind default BTREE

    /// A graph that is being deleted reports `RETIRING`. Older clients only
    /// know ACTIVE and DELETED, and a retiring graph is gone for them.
    add GraphStatus.RETIRING downgrade DELETED

    /// A new error. Older clients see the conflict they already handle, with
    /// the same message and resource id.
    add CreateGraph.errors GraphNameReservedException downgrade ConflictException {
        message <- message
        resourceId <- name
    }

    /// The revert endpoint moved under the history sub-path. The old route
    /// keeps working for older clients only.
    move RevertGraph from POST "/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/graphs/{graphId}/revert"

    // ---- hooked ------------------------------------------------------------

    /// A request from an older client may omit homeRegion; it meant the
    /// organization's home region. Needs a lookup, so it is async.
    require CreateGraph.input.homeRegion by async hook

    /// sizeBytes and indexBytes became one `storage` structure. GraphData is
    /// only ever returned, so only a downgrade is generated.
    reshape GraphData { sizeBytes, indexBytes } -> storage by hook

    /// The group filter takes several groups. A request from an older client
    /// names at most one. ListGraphs input only, so only an upgrade is generated.
    reshape ListGraphs.input { groupId } -> groupIds by hook

    /// GetWrite is gone; older clients keep it through a legacy handler.
    remove operation GetWrite

    // ---- behaviour ---------------------------------------------------------

    /// Graphs being deleted no longer appear in listings. Not a shape change,
    /// so the handler branches on the version; declaring it generates the
    /// constant and puts it in the changelog.
    behavior ListGraphs.excludesRetiring

    sunset "2028-11-01"
}
